   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Two times in one sentence",
     "texto": [
      "The part with **si** and the result do not always speak of the same time:\n\n- **Past → present**: **Si hubiera aceptado** la beca, **ahora viviría** en otra ciudad.\n- **Present → past**: **Si fuera** menos tímido, **habría solicitado** el puesto.\n\nIn the first, the cause happened in the past and the effect reaches today. In the second, a trait of today explains something that happened before."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Three mixed combinations",
     "texto": [
      "The three usual patterns are still useful. Mixed combinations add a contrast of time; they do not replace them.\n\n- **Past condition → present result**: si + pluperfect subjunctive, and conditional. **Si hubiera aceptado** la beca, **ahora viviría** en otra ciudad.\n- **Present condition → past result**: si + imperfect subjunctive, and conditional perfect. **Si fuera** más prudente, **no habría firmado**.\n- **Past condition → future result**: **Si hubieras reservado** antes, **viajarías** con nosotros mañana.\n\nThe part with **si** uses the imperfect or pluperfect subjunctive. The result uses the conditional or the conditional perfect, according to its time."
     ],
